DPIA outline and priority DPA clause

A. DPIA outline — AI-assisted applicant ranking

Owner: Each employer controller, supported by TalentBridge under Article 28. TalentBridge should maintain a product-level assessment and evidence pack that customers can adapt to their recruitment context.

1. Description of the processing

Map the flow from applicant submission through EU hosting, feature extraction, US API processing, scoring, recruiter display, final decision and deletion.

Record data categories, sources, data subjects, approximate volume, frequency, locations, access roles, vendors, sub-processors and transfer mechanism.

Document the model version, vacancy criteria, scoring logic, output explanation, confidence/limitations, override mechanism and change-management process.

State explicitly that the baseline prohibits automatic rejection and model training on applicant inputs or outputs.

2. Necessity and proportionality

Define the legitimate recruitment objective and compare AI ranking with less intrusive alternatives, including structured recruiter review.

Confirm the Article 6 basis for each purpose; complete an LIA for ranking if Article 6(1)(f) is proposed.

Test whether all input fields and derived features are necessary; redact photographs and unrelated special-category data before scoring.

Confirm transparency content, a non-AI review route, rights procedures, retention/deletion and meaningful human oversight.

Review applicable Member State employment law, collective-agreement or worker-representation requirements under Article 88.

